s=s.replace('test_antarctica_runtime.js, and test_antarctica_speech.js.', 'test_antarctica_runtime.js, test_antarctica_speech.js, and test_antarctica_hazards.js.')
s+='\nSUPER BLIZZARD AND HAZARD TUTORIAL\nAfter James\'s first station conversation, the suit announces exactly: WEATHER WARNING! SUPER BLIZZARD INCOMING! Enter / LEARN ABOUT HAZARDS opens five narrator lessons about visibility, suit heat, stamina, the beacon/map and shelter. Captions stay until you press NEXT; the final step restores movement. Lesson progress and warning state save per Wanderer and resume through Continue. Exposure and storm time are frozen during conversations, the tutorial, pauses and the map. Existing saves that completed the station conversation receive the tutorial when continued.\nThe warning and new narrator lessons use an optional temporary browser system voice because no recordings for these lines have been supplied. NARRATION / OFF keeps captions. The original Milky Way narrator recordings are unchanged. NOSTRAVECTOR_Hazard_Script.txt contains the new script.\nThe storm reduces visibility and strengthens wind-driven snow for 300 seconds of active free-roam play. SUIT HEAT drains from 100 to zero after 180 seconds exposed to this storm, restores at 1.2 points per second inside the station, and at 0.6 points per second in the occupied rover. At zero heat, the suit performs emergency recovery, returning both characters to the station interior with 35 heat. The rover remains where it was parked. The storm timer and heat are saved per character. Shelter recovery continues after the storm clears.\n'
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
